From 0c869694d54671a6af32a42cafc7daf36e2d82b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:28:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lvl-6 Enchant, and the rule that says a button the client
 draws does nothing

THE SPELL WAS ALWAYS IN THE INTERFACE. magic.if has drawn it since this fork
began, as [com_549] with its unpacked name, carrying Jagex's own checks:

    script1=gt,0    cosmic runes
    script2=gt,19   fire runes
    script3=gt,19   earth runes
    script4=gt,86   magic level
    action=Enchant Lvl-6 Jewelry

Level 87, 20 fire, 20 earth, 1 cosmic - which is the wiki's spell, arrived at
from the other direction. Ring of stone and Amulet of fury are in the obj pack
with their real names, the spotanim enchant_amulet2_lvl6 and the synths
enchant_onyx_ring and enchant_onyx_amulet are in their packs, and onyx rings,
necklaces and amulets have all been craftable at tier 6 of the jewellery ladder
the whole time. Only the id, the dbrow and the trigger were missing, so clicking
the button did nothing at all - no error, no log line, no failing check.

That is the third time: Trollheim, Bones to Peaches and Ape Atoll were the same
shape, and each was found by accident while looking at something else.

THE XP IS NOT A GUESS. The five rows above are 175, 370, 590, 670 and 780, and
the wiki's figures for those spells are 17.5, 37, 59, 67 and 78. The scale is
this table's, so the wiki's 97 becomes 970 by arithmetic. The battery checks the
whole sequence rather than the one number.

NO BERSERKER NECKLACE, and that is the honest answer to the bug-list line. There
is no such obj anywhere in this cache. The onyx necklace's own description is "I
wonder if this is valuable" where the strung amulet's is "I wonder if I can get
this enchanted" - the amulet was enchantable at this revision and the necklace
was not. Importing one is an art round like the slayer helmets, not a row here,
and a check holds the door: if a berserker_necklace obj ever appears in
obj.pack, the battery goes red and asks for the row.

The amulet's ANIM is the one inferred thing and it is flagged in the row's
comment. The amulet2 family runs human_enchantamuletlvl1 at lvl4 and lvl2 at
lvl5, so lvl6 takes lvl3. Its spotanim is the cache's own.

RULE 23 IS THE GENERAL VERSION. A spellbook button drawn from a magic sprite
sheet, carrying a real action, that no trigger in any .rs2 names. It found four
more the hour it was written - Teleother Lumbridge, Teleother Falador, Teleother
Camelot and Tele Block, all genuinely unbuilt - and they are declared with a
reason each in tools/unwiredspells.json, so the rule is green today and goes red
on the NEXT one rather than on the backlog.

IT ALSO FOUND THE REAL ANCIENT SPELLBOOK. scripts/interfaces/inter_267.if is the
377 cache's own Ancient Magicks panel: Jagex's grid, the level tooltips ("Level
94 : Ice Barrage"), all 16 combat spells and all 8 ancient teleports. The server
does not use it. ancient_magic.if is a hand-built reconstruction with an invented
layout, written when this file could not be found - and it could not be found
because an interface that IS the ancient spellbook contains no searchable word,
every component being com_<n>. magic_combat_debug.rs2 still calls the real one
"unidentifiable". Swapping to it is its own round; it is named in the spec and in
the doc rather than quietly excused.

tools/interfaceindex.py is the answer to that whole class: it prints each
unidentified interface's player-visible strings, so 133 interfaces read as a list
of features instead of a list of numbers. inter_110 is a fractional still,
inter_113 a temple repair, inter_267 the ancient book.

WHY obtainable.py NEVER SAID ANY OF THIS. Both enchanted onyx objs are defined
only in scripts/_unpack/377/all.obj, so the sweep files them under "the 377
cache's own, which this server has no content for" - a 2,713-item bucket it never
prints. That label is wrong for an item whose whole family is wired. The sweep is
not changed here; the new rule covers the case from the other end, and the doc
records the blind spot.

rs2check 0 ERROR 0 CHECK, selftest PASS on all 22 rules, thirteen batteries PASS,
33 enchant mutations each caught by its own check, mutate_labels clean on the new
harness. Not built: npm still 403s on zod, so CI's pack job is the build.

